#!/usr/bin/env node
/*
 * DK STORE: server, database and the finished React website in ONE file.
 * Customer accounts, admin dashboard, stock, revenue and PDF receipts.
 * No npm install needed to RUN it. Requires Node.js 22.13 or newer.
 *
 * HOW TO RUN (VS Code)
 *   1. Open this file's folder in VS Code (File > Open Folder).
 *   2. Optional: create a file called .env next to this file with lines like:
 *        PORT=3000
 *        ADMIN_EMAIL=you@example.com
 *        ADMIN_PASSWORD=choose-a-strong-password
 *        WHATSAPP=923141993887
 *        COOKIE_SECURE=1        (only when the site runs on https)
 *      If ADMIN_PASSWORD is empty, a random one is printed once in the terminal.
 *   3. In the terminal run:   node dk-store.cjs
 *   4. Store: http://localhost:3000     Admin: http://localhost:3000/admin.html
 *
 * EDITING THE REACT SITE
 *   The readable React source is in the dk-store-react project (src/ folder).
 *   After changing it run  npm run build  and this server automatically serves the new ./dist
 *   folder instead of the embedded copy. Delete ./dist to go back to the embedded copy.
 *
 * The database is created next to this file in a folder called data (set DATA_DIR to move it).
 * Back up data/store.db regularly. Stock starts at 0: add stock in the admin dashboard.
 *
 * FILE MAP (search for these headings)
 *   1. DATABASE   2. LOGIN AND SECURITY   3. SHOP LOGIC   4. PDF RECEIPTS
 *   5. SERVER AND API ROUTES   6. EMBEDDED REACT BUILD AND IMAGES
 */
